{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0671b268d93ea651a0a351e525bc4695b9a04cc12412b557fc0d66af3e12757a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributions are welcome and setup for development is documented in .github/development.md."},{"claim_ids":["clm_067cbf8536c1bb049b1ef5affd32f37cc54f39af436b1cf3d3dab38b70fff627"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool builds the project to detect what broke after a dependency bump, then uses ts-morph to build an AST of the code and obtain type definitions for external methods."},{"claim_ids":["clm_24adb78441e4d943d442e45b9ee6d41cfd161b2e80cc65dbf5325f1b679411cc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"bumpgen relies on build errors, so behavioral changes that don't produce build errors go undetected."},{"claim_ids":["clm_500ceac0eecbdb80ead5f18294a98f8e11d857a8a07d5858732f03a2c22f8cfc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The plan graph, the error, and the file containing the breaking change are passed to the LLM as context to maximize its ability to fix the issue."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7b28559f3a71e2ab0fee914ae754d3ca73f2453c56933e9b029a720f1c82631a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"bumpgen requires an OpenAI API key and only supports the gpt-4-turbo-preview model at this time."},{"claim_ids":["clm_801a07e51f0af58a4857e24a99b6f6372bd7cad91779bc1304c0e6ce2b78ff50"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"bumpgen creates a plan-graph DAG, based on Microsoft's codeplan paper, to execute changes in order and propagate fixes for second-order breakages across the codebase."},{"claim_ids":["clm_85cdd73eaaa0530f55fc31a2eb585b3ee0300af95e1d7666da8bcbd777284885"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"bumpgen upgrades TypeScript/TSX dependencies and makes code changes automatically when the upgrade breaks things."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a10ec0d61ea6394c831623a41ed8424b1491431675edc570712caae38325f4a0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI accepts a package name and target version (e.g. bumpgen @tanstack/react-query 5.28.14), can be run without arguments to pick a package from a menu, and offers --help for options."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bdb5b21184d1a2b4e1c5ffe4819fd0ea82a70716ed3144b885d8470837a864ec"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"bumpgen cannot handle multiple packages at once, failing on upgrades needing simultaneous peer-dependency updates, and struggles with very large framework upgrades like vue 2 to 3."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ccd43d9f1943141113d18c83d92287cad6bb0477e372f2d419de896beb673ec3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The example GitHub workflow grants pull-requests:read and contents:write permissions and passes path, llm_key, and github_token inputs to the bumpgen action."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d93adaef855c9fe4ac22f3e91846228d9666f035ec05f1c1bc0040f410905235"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A GitHub action runs bumpgen, intended to trigger on dependabot or renovatebot PRs, committing fixes to the PR branch when breaking changes are detected."},{"claim_ids":["clm_dcdd4b5e64d3c0f445f526367a3ebde2bb42740cbd6965f90c16eddfd3ee6eba"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"bumpgen with GPT-4 Turbo scored 45% (67 tasks) on a benchmark suite of version bumps with breaking changes (swe-bump-bench), with evals published in that repo."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0671b268d93ea651a0a351e525bc4695b9a04cc12412b557fc0d66af3e12757a","clm_067cbf8536c1bb049b1ef5affd32f37cc54f39af436b1cf3d3dab38b70fff627","clm_24adb78441e4d943d442e45b9ee6d41cfd161b2e80cc65dbf5325f1b679411cc","clm_500ceac0eecbdb80ead5f18294a98f8e11d857a8a07d5858732f03a2c22f8cfc","clm_7b28559f3a71e2ab0fee914ae754d3ca73f2453c56933e9b029a720f1c82631a","clm_801a07e51f0af58a4857e24a99b6f6372bd7cad91779bc1304c0e6ce2b78ff50","clm_85cdd73eaaa0530f55fc31a2eb585b3ee0300af95e1d7666da8bcbd777284885","clm_a10ec0d61ea6394c831623a41ed8424b1491431675edc570712caae38325f4a0","clm_bdb5b21184d1a2b4e1c5ffe4819fd0ea82a70716ed3144b885d8470837a864ec","clm_ccd43d9f1943141113d18c83d92287cad6bb0477e372f2d419de896beb673ec3","clm_d93adaef855c9fe4ac22f3e